  "releaseNotes": "3.0.0 — Index maintenance is now complete and appending is no longer quadratic.\n      Rows are threaded into every index rather than only the primary key, entry\n      counts are kept current (Access answers COUNT(*) and MAX from an index),\n      delete and update move or remove entries instead of leaving them behind, and\n      leaves, prefix-compressed pages and full nodes all split correctly — including\n      in trees Access wrote, where the new root used to be recorded against the wrong\n      index because Access does not order a TDEF's index-data blocks to match its\n      slots. New: creating secondary indexes (ascending or descending, single or\n      composite, backfilled), uniqueness enforced on insert, definitions spanning\n      several pages, and reading multi-value and memo-history complex columns.\n      Inserting now uses the table's free-space map instead of reading every page it\n      owns. Breaking: IndexWriter's per-index methods take an Index rather than an\n      ordinal, and Database.Create refuses .accdb rather than writing Jet 4 under an\n      ACE name. See CHANGELOG.md.",
